  "raw_text": " Set up the equation based on the given information.\nLet $x$ be the number of students who paid $\\$3.72$.\nSince there are seven students in total, the number of students who paid $\\$3.71$ is $7 - x$.\n\nStep 2: Formulate the equation for the total cost.\nThe total cost of the pizza is $\\$26.00$.\nThe cost paid by students paying $\\$3.72$ is $3.72x$.\nThe cost paid by students paying $\\$3.71$ is $3.71(7-x)$.\nSo, the sum of these costs equals the total cost:\n$3.72x + 3.71(7-x) = 26$\n\nStep 3: Solve the equation for $x$.\nDistribute the 3.71 into the parenthesis:\n$3.72x + 25.97 - 3.71x = 26$\n\nCombine like terms ($3.72x - 3.71x$):\n$(3.72 - 3.71)x + 25.97 = 26$\n$0.01x + 25.97 = 26$\n\nSubtract 25.97 from both sides:\n$0.01x = 26 - 25.97$\n$0.01x = 0.03$\n\nDivide by 0.01 to isolate $x$:\n$x = \\frac{0.03}{0.01}$\n$x = 3$\n\nStep 4: Verify the solution and determine the final answer.\nIf $x=3$, then 3 students paid $\\$3.72$.\nThe remaining students is $7-3=4$. These 4 students paid $\\$3.71$.\nCheck the total amount: $3 \\times 3.72 + 4 \\times 3.71$.\n$3 \\times 3.72 = 11.16$\n$4 \\times 3.71 = 14.84$\nSum: $11.16 + 14.84 = 26.00$.\nThe calculation matches the given total cost.\nThus, the number of students who paid $\\$3.72$ is 3.\n\nFinal Answer seems to be 3.\nDouble check the format requirements.\nNative Thinking block.\nStart immediately with Step 1: followed by mathematical work.\nStart each later section on a new line as Step 2:, Step 3:, and so on.\nEach number used exactly once.\nNever quote instructions.\nDo not box intermediate results.\nAfter closing the thinking block output exactly one line: Final answer: \\boxed{answer}.\n\nWait, the prompt says \"Begin immediately with Step 1: followed by mathematical work\". It also says \"Start each later section on a new line as Step 2:, Step 3:, and so on\".\nIt does not say I should write \"Step 1:\" on its own line or follow specific formatting other than \"Step X:\".\nI will ensure st